349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 211 0 R
/T (The Role-Specific AI Voice Assistant Framework is a new, self-contained academic prototype developed as part of this project. It is not a replacement for, or extension of, any existing production assistant, but is designed to demonstrate how a single conversational-AI backend can be parameterized to serve multiple organizational roles. The system follows a client-server, layered architecture in which users interact with the assistant through a web-based voice/chat interface; a backend server processes speech, recognizes intent, executes the mapped workflow, and returns a response, while a database persists role profiles, users, conversations, and integration configuration.)
/E (The Role-Specific AI Voice Assistant Framework is a new, self-contained academic prototype developed as part of this project. It is not a replacement for, or extension of, any existing production assistant, but is designed to demonstrate how a single conversational-AI backend can be parameterized to serve multiple organizational roles. The system follows a client-server, layered architecture in which users interact with the assistant through a web-based voice/chat interface; a backend server processes speech, recognizes intent, executes the mapped workflow, and returns a response, while a database persists role profiles, users, conversations, and integration configuration.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
